      "math_academy_id": "q-65058",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "For the function $f(x,y),$ calculate $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ given that $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}=2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}).$",
      "worked_solution": "To find $\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}}$ we differentiate the given first-order partial derivative $\\frac{∂f}{∂x}$ with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{∂}^{2}f}{∂{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\frac{∂f}{∂x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})) \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})+2x\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}))\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
